        <div class="section-title">NMJ Histology & Signal Transduction Steps</div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">8. What major structural alteration occurs as a myelinated motor nerve fiber approaches a skeletal muscle fiber?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A.</strong> It doubles its myelin sheath thickness to boost current flow.</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B.</strong> It directly fuses its cytoplasm with the interior myofibrils.</div>
